<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Defs_L2_3_2" targetNamespace="https://teck.example/process-models/pillar-03">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collab_L2_3_2">
    <bpmn:participant id="Pool_L2_3_2" name="3.2 Concentration (Flotation) (L2)" processRef="Process_L2_3_2"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_L2_3_2" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>L2 Process Area. Selective separation of valuable minerals (chalcopyrite, sphalerite, galena, molybdenite) from gangue using froth flotation. Air bubbles attach to hydrophobic mineral surfaces made selective by reagents; the loaded froth overflows to concentrate while depressed gangue reports to tailings. This is the primary value-creation process in the plant — metal recovery and concentrate grade are the defining performance variables. Circuit architecture varies by commodity.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_L2_3_2">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L2_3_2_ops" name="Control Room Operator / Metallurgist / DCS">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L2_3_2_s</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_L2_3_2_gz</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_L2_3_2_gp</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L2_3_2_e</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L2_3_2_s" name="Cyclone overflow at flotation feed sump">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_3_2_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_1" name="3.2.1 Reagent Management">
      <bpmn:documentation>L3/L0 Process. Chemical reagents are the primary selectivity control mechanism in flotation. Collectors attach to target mineral surfaces; frothers stabilise bubble-particle aggregates in the froth; depressants prevent non-target minerals from floating; pH modifiers (lime) control pulp chemistry to enable selective activation and depression.
ISA-95 level: 0–3
Actors: Metallurgist; Control Room Operator; DCS
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0–3; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2
DDVC layer: Raw; Curated (reagent_addition_record)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_3_2_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_3_2_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_2" name="3.2.2 Copper Flotation Circuit">
      <bpmn:documentation>[COPPER-SPECIFIC] Applies to: QB, HVC, Antamina (Cu circuit first), CdA. L0/L1/L2 Process. The Cu flotation circuit selectively recovers chalcopyrite (CuFeS₂) and bornite (Cu₅FeS₄) from the ground slurry into a high-grade Cu concentrate. The circuit typically comprises rougher, scavenger, and cleaner stages in a standard rougher-scavenger-cleaner (RSC) configuration, with regrinding of cleaner tails or scavenger concentrate where liberation is insufficient.
ISA-95 level: 0–2
Actors: Control Room Operator; Metallurgist; DCS
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0–2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2, 5, 6, 7
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series); Curated (concentrate_production_record)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_3_2_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_3_2_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_L2_3_2_gz" name="Zn circuit fitted?" default="Flow_L2_3_2_5">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_3_2_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_3_2_4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_3_2_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_3" name="3.2.3 Zinc Flotation Circuit">
      <bpmn:documentation>[ZINC-SPECIFIC — where applicable] Applies to: Antamina (sequential after Cu), Red Dog (primary Zn circuit). L0/L1/L2 Process. At polymetallic operations, the Cu flotation tailings (or primary mill product at Red Dog) feed the Zn flotation circuit. Sphalerite (ZnS) must first be activated with copper sulphate (CuSO₄) before it becomes floatable — it is naturally depressed in the Cu circuit. The Zn circuit follows the same RSC architecture as the Cu circuit.
ISA-95 level: 0–2
Actors: Control Room Operator; Metallurgist; DCS
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0–2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2, 5, 6, 7
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series); Curated (concentrate_production_record — Zn)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_3_2_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_3_2_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_L2_3_2_gp" name="Pb circuit active?" default="Flow_L2_3_2_8">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_3_2_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_3_2_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_3_2_7</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_3_2_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_4" name="3.2.4 Lead Flotation Circuit">
      <bpmn:documentation>[LEAD-SPECIFIC — where applicable] Applies to: Antamina (where Pb circuit is activated), Red Dog. L0/L1/L2 Process. At polymetallic operations with galena (PbS), a lead flotation circuit follows the Zn circuit (or in some designs, precedes it in a Cu-Pb-Zn sequential circuit). At Red Dog, Pb and Zn are separated by differential flotation — Pb is floated first at low pH (Pb selectivity over sphalerite), then Zn is activated and floated.
ISA-95 level: 0–2
Actors: Control Room Operator; Metallurgist; DCS
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0–2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2, 5, 6, 7
DDVC layer: Raw; Curated (concentrate_production_record — Pb)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_3_2_7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_3_2_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L2_3_2_e" name="Composites to LIMS; concentrate to thickeners">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_3_2_8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_3_2_9</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_3_2_1" sourceRef="Start_L2_3_2_s" targetRef="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_3_2_2" sourceRef="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_1" targetRef="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_3_2_3" sourceRef="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_2" targetRef="Gw_L2_3_2_gz"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_3_2_4" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_L2_3_2_gz" targetRef="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_3_2_5" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_L2_3_2_gz" targetRef="Gw_L2_3_2_gp"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_3_2_6" sourceRef="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_3" targetRef="Gw_L2_3_2_gp"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_3_2_7" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_L2_3_2_gp" targetRef="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_4"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_3_2_8" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_L2_3_2_gp" targetRef="End_L2_3_2_e"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_3_2_9" sourceRef="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_4" targetRef="End_L2_3_2_e"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_L2_3_2">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_L2_3_2" bpmnElement="Collab_L2_3_2">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Pool_L2_3_2_di" bpmnElement="Pool_L2_3_2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="20" y="20" width="1334" height="510"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L2_3_2_ops_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L2_3_2_ops" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="20" width="1294" height="510"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_L2_3_2_s_di" bpmnElement="Start_L2_3_2_s"><dc:Bounds x="110" y="247" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="88" y="309" width="100" height="56"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_1_di" bpmnElement="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_1" isExpanded="false"><dc:Bounds x="202" y="227" width="170" height="96"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_2_di" bpmnElement="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_2" isExpanded="false"><dc:Bounds x="408" y="227" width="170" height="96"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gw_L2_3_2_gz_di" bpmnElement="Gw_L2_3_2_gz" isMarkerVisible="true"><dc:Bounds x="614" y="240" width="70" height="70"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="599" y="206" width="100" height="28"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_3_di" bpmnElement="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_3" isExpanded="false"><dc:Bounds x="720" y="397" width="170" height="96"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gw_L2_3_2_gp_di" bpmnElement="Gw_L2_3_2_gp" isMarkerVisible="true"><dc:Bounds x="926" y="240" width="70" height="70"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="855" y="206" width="100" height="28"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_4_di" bpmnElement="Sub_L2_3_2_3_2_4" isExpanded="false"><dc:Bounds x="1032" y="57" width="170" height="96"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_L2_3_2_e_di" bpmnElement="End_L2_3_2_e"><dc:Bounds x="1238" y="247" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1216" y="309" width="100" height="70"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_3_2_1_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_3_2_1"><di:waypoint x="166" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="202" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_3_2_2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_3_2_2"><di:waypoint x="372" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="408" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_3_2_3_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_3_2_3"><di:waypoint x="578" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="614" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_3_2_4_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_3_2_4"><di:waypoint x="649" y="310"/><di:waypoint x="649" y="445"/><di:waypoint x="720" y="445"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="655" y="314" width="27" height="14"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_3_2_5_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_3_2_5"><di:waypoint x="684" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="926" y="275"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="688" y="255" width="21" height="14"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_3_2_6_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_3_2_6"><di:waypoint x="890" y="445"/><di:waypoint x="961" y="445"/><di:waypoint x="961" y="310"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_3_2_7_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_3_2_7"><di:waypoint x="961" y="240"/><di:waypoint x="961" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="1032" y="105"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="967" y="222" width="27" height="14"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_3_2_8_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_3_2_8"><di:waypoint x="996" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="1238" y="275"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1000" y="255" width="21" height="14"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_3_2_9_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_3_2_9"><di:waypoint x="1202" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="1266" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="1266" y="247"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
